## Flags for the VM inside the troupe binary, rendered once per Burrito target.
<%= if String.starts_with?(System.get_env("BURRITO_TARGET", ""), "windows") do %>
## Windows (#231, TUI Decision 128). The console belongs to troupe, not to the VM, and
## Burrito's launcher in front of the VM dies of any Ctrl-C the console signals, whatever
## the VM does: the VM must never be what is left behind in the shell's console.
##
## -noinput: no reader on the console. The terminal UI reads its own keys, and a reader
## beside it takes some of them; a question `troupe config` asks starts one
## (`Troupe.CLI.Prompt`).
## +Bc: while troupe runs, the console makes a key of Ctrl-C, not a signal, so nothing
## dies of it and nothing opens the break handler's menu; the terminal UI reads it. A
## Ctrl-C another program signals ends the VM, as it ends the launcher.
-noinput
+Bc
<% end %>
